                <pb facs="0762" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Tri-Motors Safety Airways/146:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-19T14:00:00+00:00">October 19, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 19—10:20 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>483. Reference Department’s telegram 316, October 1, 6 p.m. Orally informed by
                    Ministry for Foreign Affairs as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Authorization accorded for two months provided that during that period
                            there shall be concluded an accord looking to cooperation between French
                            Aéropostale and the New York, Rio, and Buenos Aires Lines and the Pan
                            American Airways. Further the New York, Rio, Buenos Aires planes not to
                            carry photographic apparatus nor to fly over zone of Fort de
                            France.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
